{"id":50290,"ord":84,"n_segments":142,"prev":50289,"next":50291,"doc":{"id":"66086","title":"66086_Zilner T. Randolph oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Zilner T. Randolph","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/66086/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=66086"},"chapter":"The 1931 tour, records and break-up","title":"Teddy Wilson, Yank Porter and the Oldham brothers in the 1933 band","category":"person_portrait","summary":"Randolph hired Teddy Wilson from Chicago, along with Yank Porter, the Johnson brothers and the Oldham brothers.","period":"1933","year_from":1933,"year_to":1933,"words":165,"start":[116,12],"end":[118,5],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=66086#s50290","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[{"name":"Ritz-Carlton","focus":0,"city":"Chicago"}],"bands":[{"name":"Louis Armstrong Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Louis Armstrong"}]},"people":[{"name":"Teddy Wilson","qid":"Q506052","n":6},{"name":"Jimmy Noone","qid":"Q492247","n":3},{"name":"Yank Porter","qid":"Q2586885","n":2},{"name":"Louis Armstrong","qid":"Q1779","n":1},{"name":"Johnson Brothers","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":116,"b":12,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yeah, '34 band. Now, the '33 band, I think, is the one I had Teddy Wilson in."},{"p":116,"b":13,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Yes. Yes."},{"p":116,"b":14,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yes."},{"p":116,"b":15,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"I think they were his first recor-"},{"p":117,"b":0,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"dings."},{"p":117,"b":1,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"the --"},{"p":117,"b":2,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"I had Teddy Wilson, Yank Porter of"},{"p":117,"b":3,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Yes."},{"p":117,"b":4,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yes. Yank Porter."},{"p":117,"b":5,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"And the Johnson Brothers."},{"p":117,"b":6,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yeah, that's right."},{"p":117,"b":7,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"And the Oldham Brothers."},{"p":117,"b":8,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"The Oldham Brothers, that's right."},{"p":117,"b":9,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"How did you find Teddy?"},{"p":117,"b":10,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Well, Teddy was here in the city."},{"p":117,"b":11,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Yeah, I had talked to Teddy. Teddy is a friend of mine. He said that he'd been playing with Jimmy Noone."},{"p":117,"b":12,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Uh-huh, yes."},{"p":117,"b":13,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Before he went with Louis."},{"p":117,"b":14,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yeah, that's before -- Jimmy has passed, too, hasn't he?"},{"p":117,"b":15,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Yes, yes."},{"p":117,"b":16,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Jimmy Noone has passed, yeah. Well, you know, it's been a time since I've seen Teddy, though. Teddy Wilson."},{"p":117,"b":17,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"He was in town last month."},{"p":117,"b":18,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Was he?"},{"p":117,"b":19,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"And he closed downtown at the Ritz"},{"p":118,"b":0,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Carlton."},{"p":118,"b":1,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yeah. I guess he's still playing a lot of piano."},{"p":118,"b":2,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Oh, yeah, yeah."},{"p":118,"b":3,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yeah, yeah."},{"p":118,"b":4,"s":"MR. DIMICHAEL","x":"Yeah, he's a wonderful man."},{"p":118,"b":5,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yes."}]}